---
// The Kindle differentiator gets real space on the front page, per
// specs/04-front-page.md#5-kindle-band.
//
// v1 note: the spec calls for this preview to be generated from the real
// PDF at build time (render page 3 to PNG) so it can never misrepresent
// the output. That requires a PDF-rasterization step that doesn't exist
// yet — tracked as a follow-up to story C1. This CSS-drawn mockup uses
// real content from the shipped TypeScript sheet's "At a glance" table,
// so it is representative rather than a stock illustration, but it is not
// pixel-identical to the compiled PDF.
---

<section class="kindle-band" aria-labelledby="kindle-heading">
	<div class="kindle-band-inner">
		<div class="kindle-copy">
			<h2 id="kindle-heading">Read it on your Kindle</h2>
			<p>
				Every sheet is typeset for e-ink in two sizes — Paperwhite and
				Scribe. Not a shrunken A4 PDF: real margins, grayscale-safe
				code highlighting, and type sized for a 300ppi panel.
			</p>
			<a href="/languages/typescript/" class="kindle-cta">Browse sheets →</a>
		</div>
		<div class="kindle-frame" aria-hidden="true">
			<div class="kindle-screen">
				<p class="kindle-title">TypeScript</p>
				<div class="kindle-rule"></div>
				<table class="kindle-table">
					<tr><td><code>as const</code></td><td>literal, readonly</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>satisfies T</code></td><td>check, keep type</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>keyof T</code></td><td>union of keys</td></tr>
				</table>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.kindle-band {
		background: var(--sl-color-accent-low);
		margin-block-start: 3rem;
		padding-block: 3rem;
	}

	.kindle-band-inner {
		max-width: var(--sl-content-width);
		margin-inline: auto;
		padding-inline: 1.5rem;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		gap: 2rem;
		align-items: center;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50rem) {
		.kindle-band-inner {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		}
	}

	.kindle-copy h2 {
		margin-block-start: 0;
	}

	.kindle-copy p {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		max-width: 32rem;
	}

	.kindle-cta {
		display: inline-block;
		color: var(--sl-color-accent);
		font-weight: 600;
		text-decoration: none;
	}

	.kindle-cta:hover {
		text-decoration: underline;
	}

	.kindle-frame {
		justify-self: center;
		width: 14rem;
		padding: 0.9rem;
		border-radius: 1.1rem;
		background: #2a2a2a;
		box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
	}

	.kindle-screen {
		background: #f4f4f2;
		border-radius: 0.3rem;
		padding: 1rem 0.9rem;
		aspect-ratio: 3 / 4;
		color: #1a1a1a;
	}

	.kindle-title {
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 1.1rem;
		margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
	}

	.kindle-rule {
		height: 1px;
		background: #ccc;
		margin-block-end: 0.6rem;
	}

	.kindle-table {
		width: 100%;
		font-size: 0.6rem;
		border-collapse: collapse;
	}

	.kindle-table td {
		padding: 0.25rem 0;
		border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;
		vertical-align: top;
	}

	.kindle-table td:first-child {
		font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
		padding-right: 0.5rem;
		white-space: nowrap;
	}
</style>
